var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"category":"section","location":"examples/HomobilayerTMD/#Twisted-Homobilayer-Transition-Metal-Dichalcogenides","page":"Twisted Homobilayer Transition Metal Dichalcogenides","text":"For twisted homobilayer transition metal dichalcogenides, such as the twisted bilayer WSe₂ or MoTe₂, the continuum model [Phys. Rev. Lett. 122, 086402 (2019)] has two material parameters, i.e., a₀ (monolayer lattice constant), and m (effective mass of the conduction band), one device parameter, i.e., θ (twist angle), and five phenomenological parameters, i.e., Vᶻ (perpendicular displacement field), μ (chemical potential), V (amplitude of Moire potential), ψ (phase of Moire potential), and w (interlayer hopping amplitude).","title":"Twisted Homobilayer Transition Metal Dichalcogenides"},{"category":"section","location":"examples/HomobilayerTMD/#Trivial-Band-Topology","page":"Twisted Homobilayer Transition Metal Dichalcogenides","text":"The band topology of the Moire bands depends on the aforementioned parameters. For a typical set of parameters [Phys. Rev. Research 2, 033087 (2020)] that may be related to twisted bilayer WSe₂, the topmost Moire band is topologically trivial.\n\nFirst, we calculate the energy bands with such a set of parameters in both valleys:\n\nusing MoireSuperlattices\nusing Plots\nusing QuantumLattices\nusing TightBindingApproximation\n\n# `a₀`: monolayer lattice constant (Å)\n# `m`: effective mass of the conduction band (mₑ)\n# `θ`: twist angle (°)\n# `Vᶻ`: perpendicular displacement field (meV)\n# `μ`: chemical potential (meV)\n# `V`: amplitude of Moire potential (meV)\n# `ψ`: phase of Moire potential (°)\n# `w`: interlayer hopping amplitude (meV)\nparameters = (a₀=3.28, m=0.45, θ=3.70, Vᶻ=0.0, μ=0.0, V=4.4, ψ=5.9, w=20.0)\nWSe₂ = Algorithm(:WSe₂, BLTMD(values(parameters)...; truncation=4), parameters)\nrecipls = WSe₂.frontend.reciprocallattice.translations\nbands₁ = WSe₂(:EB, EnergyBands(ReciprocalPath(recipls, hexagon\"Γ-K₁-M₁-Γ\", length=100)))\nbands₂ = WSe₂(:EB, EnergyBands(ReciprocalPath(recipls, hexagon\"Γ-K₄-M₄-Γ\", length=100)))\n\nemin, emax = -100.0, 30.0\nplt = plot()\nplot!(plt, bands₁, ylim=(emin, emax), color=\"blue\", title=\"\")\nplot!(plt, bands₂, ylim=(emin, emax), color=\"blue\", title=\"\")\n\nThe bands are two-fold degenerate due to the valley degrees of freedom. Note that due to the spin-valley lock in WSe₂, such a degeneracy can also be viewed as the spin degeneracy.\n\nThen we compute the Berry curvature and Chern number of the topmost Moire band:\n\nberry = WSe₂(:BC, BerryCurvature(BrillouinZone(recipls, 48), [dimension(WSe₂)]))\nplot(berry)\n\nThe perpendicular displacement field can induce a layer dependent potential, which will lead to the splitting of the two spins:\n\nupdate!(WSe₂; Vᶻ=8.0)\nbands₁ = WSe₂(:EB, EnergyBands(ReciprocalPath(recipls, hexagon\"Γ-K₁-M₁-Γ\", length=100)))\nbands₂ = WSe₂(:EB, EnergyBands(ReciprocalPath(recipls, hexagon\"Γ-K₄-M₄-Γ\", length=100)))\n\nplt = plot()\nplot!(plt, bands₁, ylim=(emin, emax), color=\"blue\", title=\"\")\nplot!(plt, bands₂, ylim=(emin, emax), color=\"blue\", title=\"\")\n\nFor the topologically trivial topmost Moire band, it forms a triangular lattice. The effective tight-binding model of this sole band can be obtained:\n\nlattice = MoireTriangular(6)\nhilbert = Hilbert(Fock{:f}(1, 2), length(lattice))\nwannier = MoireWannier(WSe₂, lattice; nk=24)\nhopping = HoppingIntegral(wannier)\ntba = Algorithm(:tba, TBA(lattice, hilbert, terms(hopping; tol=10^-6)))\nnothing # hide\n\nHere, the hopping parameters are truncated up to the 6th order. We can compare the energy bands of this tight-binding model with those of the continuum model:\n\nbands₃ = tba(:EB, EnergyBands(ReciprocalPath(recipls, hexagon\"Γ-K-M-Γ\", length=100)))\nplt = plot()\nplot!(plt, bands₁, ylim=(emin, emax), color=\"blue\", title=\"\")\nplot!(plt, bands₂, ylim=(emin, emax), color=\"blue\", title=\"\")\nplot!(plt, bands₃, ylim=(emin, emax), color=\"red\", lw=4, alpha=0.3, title=\"\")","title":"Trivial Band Topology"},{"category":"section","location":"examples/HomobilayerTMD/#Nontrivial-Band-Topology","page":"Twisted Homobilayer Transition Metal Dichalcogenides","text":"With another set of parameters [Phys. Rev. Lett. 132, 036501 (2024)] that was proposed to be suitable for twisted bilayer MoTe₂, the top two Moire bands have opposite Chern numbers.\n\nFirst, we calculate the energy bands with such a set of parameters in a single valley:\n\nusing MoireSuperlattices\nusing Plots\nusing QuantumLattices\nusing TightBindingApproximation\n\nparameters = (a₀=3.52, m=0.6, θ=3.89, Vᶻ=0.0, μ=30.0, V=20.8, ψ=107.7, w=-23.8)\nMoTe₂ = Algorithm(:MoTe₂, BLTMD(values(parameters)...; truncation=4), parameters)\nrecipls = MoTe₂.frontend.reciprocallattice.translations\nbands = MoTe₂(:EB, EnergyBands(ReciprocalPath(recipls, hexagon\"Γ-K₁-M₁-Γ\", length=100)))\nplot(bands, ylim=(-50.0, 10.0), color=\"blue\", title=\"\")\n\nThen we compute the Berry curvature and Chern numbers of the top two Moire bands:\n\nberry = MoTe₂(\n    :BC, BerryCurvature(BrillouinZone(recipls, 48), [dimension(MoTe₂), dimension(MoTe₂)-1])\n)\nplot(berry)","title":"Nontrivial Band Topology"},{"category":"section","location":"examples/Visualization/#Visualization-of-Moire-Superlattices-by-Twist","page":"Visualization of Moire Superlattices by Twist","text":"Here follows a quick view of the commensurate Moire superlattices composed of twisted homobilayer graphene:\n\nusing MoireSuperlattices\nusing Plots\n\nanim = @animate for i ∈ 2:10\n    plot(\n        CommensurateBilayerHoneycomb((i, 1)), :real, 30;\n        xlim=(-50, 50), ylim=(-30, 30), axis=false, size=(600, 400), vector=false\n    )\nend\ngif(anim; fps=1.5)\n\nThe crystal structure of a commensurate Moire superlattice composed of twisted homobilayer graphene is characterized by two coprime positive integers (m, r) [Phys. Rev. B 86, 155449 (2012)]. In general, we need to distinguish two cases, i.e., whether gcd(r, 3) is 1 or 3, where gcd denotes the greatest common divisor.","title":"Visualization of Moire Superlattices by Twist"},{"category":"section","location":"examples/Visualization/#When-gcd(r,-3)-is-1","page":"Visualization of Moire Superlattices by Twist","text":"For example, m=8, r=1:\n\nplot(CommensurateBilayerHoneycomb((8, 1)), :real; xlim=(-20, 20), ylim=(-10, 20))\n\nIn the reciprocal space, the K points of the top and bottom layers correspond to two inequivalent K points of the Moire Brillouin zone:\n\nplot(CommensurateBilayerHoneycomb((8, 1)), :reciprocal; xlim=(-5, 5), ylim=(-4, 4))","title":"When gcd(r, 3) is 1"},{"category":"section","location":"examples/Visualization/#When-gcd(r,-3)-is-3","page":"Visualization of Moire Superlattices by Twist","text":"For example, m=20, r=3:\n\nplot(CommensurateBilayerHoneycomb((20, 3)), :real; xlim=(-20, 20), ylim=(-10, 20))\n\nIn the reciprocal space, the K points of the top and bottom layers correspond to two equivalent K points of the Moire Brillouin zone:\n\nplot(CommensurateBilayerHoneycomb((20, 3)), :reciprocal; xlim=(-5, 5), ylim=(-4, 4))","title":"When gcd(r, 3) is 3"},{"category":"section","location":"examples/Introduction/#examples","page":"Introduction","text":"Here are some examples to illustrate how this package could be used.\n\nPages = [\n        \"Visualization.md\",\n        \"HomobilayerTMD.md\",\n        ]\nDepth = 2","title":"Introduction"},{"category":"type","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.BLTMD","page":"Manual","text":"BLTMD{\n    L<:MoireReciprocalLattice,\n    D<:Function,\n    S<:OperatorGenerator,\n    Q<:Quadraticization,\n    H<:CategorizedGenerator{<:OperatorSum{<:Quadratic}}\n} <: MoireSystem{NamedTuple{(:a₀, :m, :θ, :Vᶻ, :μ), NTuple{5, Float64}}, L, D, S, Q, H}\n\nTwisted transition metal dichalcogenide homobilayers.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.BLTMD"},{"category":"method","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.BLTMD-NTuple{8, Number}","page":"Manual","text":"BLTMD(a₀::Number, m::Number, θ::Number, Vᶻ::Number, μ::Number, V::Number, ψ::Number, w::Number; truncation::Int=4)\n\nContinuum model of twisted transition metal dichalcogenide homobilayers.\n\nHere, the parameters are as follows:\n\na₀: monolayer lattice constant (Å)\nm: effective mass of the conduction band (mₑ)\nθ: twist angle (°)\nVᶻ: perpendicular displacement field (meV)\nμ: chemical potential (meV)\nV: amplitude of Moire potential (meV)\nψ: phase of Moire potential (°)\nw: interlayer hopping amplitude (meV)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.BLTMD"},{"category":"type","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.BareCoulomb","page":"Manual","text":"BareCoulomb(ϵ::Real)\n\nBare (unscreened) 2D Coulomb potential: V(q) = 2π e² / (ϵ aₘ |q|). q=0 skipped (returns 0).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.BareCoulomb"},{"category":"type","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.C3","page":"Manual","text":"const C3 = C₃\n\nASCII alias for C₃.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.C3"},{"category":"type","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.CommensurateBilayerHoneycomb","page":"Manual","text":"CommensurateBilayerHoneycomb\n\nCommensurate Moire superlattice composed of two layers of honeycomb lattices.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.CommensurateBilayerHoneycomb"},{"category":"type","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.CoulombIntegral","page":"Manual","text":"CoulombIntegral{W<:MoireWannier}\n\nPrecomputed Coulomb form factor for a Wannier function.\n\nFields:\n\nwannier::W — reference to the Wannier function\nqs::Vector{SVector{2,Float64}} — unique q-vectors from the pairwise convolution\nformfactor::Vector{Matrix{ComplexF64}} — M(q)†M(q) / Nₖ² matrices at each q, (nband×nband)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.CoulombIntegral"},{"category":"type","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.CoulombIntegral-2","page":"Manual","text":"(coulomb::CoulombIntegral)(R::AbstractVector{<:Number}, potential=BareCoulomb(1.0))\n\nCompute U(R) = (1/(Nk Ω)) Σq V(|q|, aₘ) |M(q)|² e^{iq·R} in meV.\n\npotential is a callable potential(q::Real, aₘ::Real) -> Real, e.g. BareCoulomb(ϵ), ImageCoulomb(ϵ, d), TanhCoulomb(ϵ, d), or a user-defined function. Defaults to BareCoulomb(1.0) (unscreened, ε=1).\n\nReturns an nband×nband Matrix{Float64} Coulomb interaction matrix.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.CoulombIntegral"},{"category":"method","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.CoulombIntegral-Tuple{MoireWannier}","page":"Manual","text":"CoulombIntegral(wannier::MoireWannier)\n\nConstruct by computing the form factor M(q) from Bloch coefficients via pairwise convolution.\n\nAlgorithm: compute gauge-transformed Bloch coefficients cn(p) for each Wannier function n at extended momenta p=k+G, then for each pair (n,m) accumulate M{m,n}(q) = Σp dot(cn(p+q), c_m(p)). The q-mesh emerges naturally from the G/G' truncation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.CoulombIntegral"},{"category":"type","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.C₃","page":"Manual","text":"C₃ <: PointGroup\n\nThree-fold rotation symmetry (120° fundamental angle, 2π/3 rad).\n\nFor bond equivalence classification, sign uses a 60° azimuth discretization to distinguish bonds that are C₃-equivalent in the forward direction (Δ even → +1) from those that are C₃-equivalent in the reverse direction (Δ odd → -1).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.C₃"},{"category":"type","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.HoppingIntegral","page":"Manual","text":"HoppingIntegral{W<:MoireWannier}\n\nHopping amplitude calculator for a Wannier function.\n\nFields:\n\nwannier::W — reference to the MoireWannier\n\nCallable as (hopping::HoppingIntegral)(R::AbstractVector{<:Number}) -> Matrix{ComplexF64}:\n\nt_mn(R) = (1N) Σ_k exp(-ikR) U(k) diag(ε(k)) U(k)_mn\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.HoppingIntegral"},{"category":"type","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.ImageCoulomb","page":"Manual","text":"ImageCoulomb(ϵ::Real, d::Real)\n\nImage-charge screened Coulomb: V(q) = 2π e² (1 - e^{-2dₘ|q|}) / (ϵ aₘ |q|) where dₘ = d/aₘ.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.ImageCoulomb"},{"category":"type","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.MoireHoneycomb","page":"Manual","text":"MoireHoneycomb{D<:Number} <: MoireSuperlattice{C₃, D}\n\nEmergent honeycomb superlattice in Moire systems, composed of MX and XM stacking sites.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.MoireHoneycomb"},{"category":"method","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.MoireHoneycomb-Union{Tuple{Int64}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{Int64, Type{T}}} where T<:Number","page":"Manual","text":"MoireHoneycomb(truncation::Int, [T=Float64])\n\nConstruct with coordinate type T. XM at (2v₁-v₂)/3, MX at (v₁+v₂)/3.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.MoireHoneycomb"},{"category":"type","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.MoireNeighbors","page":"Manual","text":"MoireNeighbors{G<:PointGroup, D<:Number}\n\nFlat collection of symmetry-inequivalent Bond objects under point group G.\n\nUse bonds to query by neighbor order.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.MoireNeighbors"},{"category":"method","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.MoireNeighbors-Union{Tuple{Int64, Int64}, Tuple{G}} where G<:PointGroup","page":"Manual","text":"MoireNeighbors{G}(nsublattice, truncation) where {G<:PointGroup}\nMoireNeighbors{G, D}(nsublattice, truncation) where {G<:PointGroup, D<:Number}\nMoireNeighbors{G}(lattice, truncation) where {G<:PointGroup}\n\nConstructors:\n\nMoireNeighbors{G}(nsublattice, truncation) — empty, default Float64 coordinates.\nMoireNeighbors{G, D}(nsublattice, truncation) — empty, coordinate type D.\nMoireNeighbors{G}(lattice, truncation) — collect symmetry-inequivalent bonds; nsublattice from length(lattice).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.MoireNeighbors"},{"category":"type","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.MoireReciprocalLattice","page":"Manual","text":"MoireReciprocalLattice{G<:PointGroup, T<:Number} <: AbstractLattice{2, T, 0}\n\nAbstract type for Moire reciprocal lattices parameterized by point group G.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.MoireReciprocalLattice"},{"category":"type","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.MoireSpace","page":"Manual","text":"MoireSpace <: SimpleInternal{MoireSpinor{Int, Int, Int, Rational{Int}}}\n\nThe internal degrees of freedom of Moire systems.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.MoireSpace"},{"category":"type","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.MoireSpinor","page":"Manual","text":"MoireSpinor{V<:Union{Int, Colon}, L<:Union{Int, Colon}, S<:Union{Int, Colon}, P<:Union{Rational{Int}, Colon}} <: InternalIndex\n\nThe index of the internal degrees of freedom of Moire systems.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.MoireSpinor"},{"category":"type","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.MoireSuperlattice","page":"Manual","text":"MoireSuperlattice{G<:PointGroup, D<:Number} <: AbstractLattice{2, D, 2}\n\nAbstract type of the emergent superlattices in Moire systems, parameterized by point group G and coordinate type D.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.MoireSuperlattice"},{"category":"type","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.MoireSystem","page":"Manual","text":"MoireSystem{P<:Parameters, L<:MoireReciprocalLattice, D<:Function, S<:OperatorGenerator, Q<:Quadraticization, H<:CategorizedGenerator{<:OperatorSum{<:Quadratic}}} <: TBA{Fermionic{:TBA}, H, Nothing}\n\nThe continuum model of Moire systems.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.MoireSystem"},{"category":"type","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.MoireTriangular","page":"Manual","text":"MoireTriangular{D<:Number} <: MoireSuperlattice{C₃, D}\n\nEmergent triangular superlattice in Moire systems.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.MoireTriangular"},{"category":"method","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.MoireTriangular-Union{Tuple{Int64}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{Int64, Type{T}}} where T<:Number","page":"Manual","text":"MoireTriangular(truncation::Int, [T=Float64])\n\nConstruct with coordinate type T. The single site per unitcell is at the origin (MM stacking site).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.MoireTriangular"},{"category":"type","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.MoireTriangularReciprocal","page":"Manual","text":"MoireTriangularReciprocal{T<:Number} <: MoireReciprocalLattice{C₃, T}\n\nC₃-symmetric Moire reciprocal lattice with truncation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.MoireTriangularReciprocal"},{"category":"type","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.MoireWannier","page":"Manual","text":"(wannier::MoireWannier)(r::AbstractVector{<:Number}, sublattice::Int=1) -> Vector{ComplexF64}\n\nEvaluate the Wannier function at real-space position r for a given sublattice.\n\nFormula: Wₙˡ(r) = (1/N√Ω) Σ{k, G, ν} bloch{G, l, ν}(k) · U_{ν, n}(k) · e^{i(k+G)·r}, where N is the number of k-points and Ω is the volume of the unit cell in the real space.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.MoireWannier"},{"category":"type","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.MoireWannier-2","page":"Manual","text":"MoireWannier{L<:MoireSuperlattice, G<:MoireReciprocalLattice, B<:BrillouinZone}\n\nWannier function constructed on an emergent Moire superlattice.\n\nFields:\n\naₘ::Float64 — lattice constant of the moire superlattice\nlattice::L — emergent superlattice (MoireTriangular or MoireHoneycomb)\nreciprocallattice::G — truncated plane-wave basis (G-vectors) from the continuum model\nbrillouinzone::B — uniform k-point mesh over the moire Brillouin zone\nenergies::Matrix{Float64} — raw band energies, (nband, nk)\nbloch::Array{ComplexF64, 4} — raw Bloch eigenvectors, (nlayer, nG, nband, nk), pre-gauge\nU::Array{ComplexF64, 3} — gauge transformation matrices, (nband, nband, nk)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.MoireWannier"},{"category":"method","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.MoireWannier-Tuple{MoireSystem, MoireHoneycomb, QuantumLattices.Spatials.BrillouinZone}","page":"Manual","text":"MoireWannier(moiresystem::MoireSystem, lattice::MoireHoneycomb, brillouinzone::BrillouinZone; bands::UnitRange{Int}, tol::Real=atol)\n\nConstruct Wannier functions for a 2-band subspace on a honeycomb lattice.\n\nSteps:\n\nExtract raw Bloch states for the 2-band subspace\nSU(2) rotation: maximize layer polarization via diagonalizing layer projectors\nU(1) gauge fix: ψ₁(rXM) real positive (Wannier 1 at XM, bottom-layer), ψ₂(rMX) real positive (Wannier 2 at MX, top-layer)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.MoireWannier"},{"category":"method","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.MoireWannier-Tuple{MoireSystem, MoireSuperlattice}","page":"Manual","text":"MoireWannier(moiresystem::MoireSystem, lattice::MoireSuperlattice; nk=24, kwargs...)\n\nConvenience constructor that auto-generates a BrillouinZone with nk k-points per dimension from lattice and delegates to the full constructor.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.MoireWannier"},{"category":"method","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.MoireWannier-Tuple{MoireSystem, MoireTriangular, QuantumLattices.Spatials.BrillouinZone}","page":"Manual","text":"MoireWannier(moiresystem::MoireSystem, lattice::MoireTriangular, brillouinzone::BrillouinZone; band::Int=dimension(moiresystem), tol::Real=atol)\n\nConstruct the Wannier function for a single band on a triangular lattice.\n\nGauge fixing: U(1) phase such that the bottom-layer component at r=0 (MM site) is real and positive.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.MoireWannier"},{"category":"method","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.MoireWannier-Tuple{QuantumLattices.Frameworks.Algorithm{<:MoireSystem}, Vararg{Any}}","page":"Manual","text":"MoireWannier(moiresystem::Algorithm{<:MoireSystem}, args...; kwargs...)\n\nForward to the wrapped MoireSystem frontend.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.MoireWannier"},{"category":"type","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.OnsiteAmplitude","page":"Manual","text":"OnsiteAmplitude <: Function\n\nOnsite amplitude. Matches a self-bond (bondkind=0) to a specific sublattice and returns 1 (match) or 0 (no match).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.OnsiteAmplitude"},{"category":"type","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.PointGroup","page":"Manual","text":"PointGroup\n\nAbstract type for point group symmetries used to classify bond equivalence and parameterize lattice/reciprocal-lattice types.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.PointGroup"},{"category":"method","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.PointGroup-Tuple{MoireNeighbors}","page":"Manual","text":"PointGroup(neighbors::MoireNeighbors) -> PointGroup\nPointGroup(::Type{<:MoireNeighbors{G}}) where {G<:PointGroup} -> G\n\nGet the point group of MoireNeighbors from an instance or type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.PointGroup"},{"category":"method","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.PointGroup-Tuple{MoireReciprocalLattice}","page":"Manual","text":"PointGroup(moire::MoireReciprocalLattice) -> PointGroup\nPointGroup(::Type{<:MoireReciprocalLattice{G}}) where {G<:PointGroup} -> G\n\nGet the point group of a Moire reciprocal lattice from an instance or type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.PointGroup"},{"category":"method","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.PointGroup-Tuple{MoireSuperlattice}","page":"Manual","text":"PointGroup(lattice::MoireSuperlattice) -> PointGroup\nPointGroup(::Type{<:MoireSuperlattice{G}}) where {G<:PointGroup} -> G\n\nGet the point group of a Moire superlattice from an instance or type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.PointGroup"},{"category":"type","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.RealZone","page":"Manual","text":"RealZone{N, S<:SVector, V<:Number}\n\nA rectangular zone in real space.\n\nAlias for ReciprocalZone with the space-type parameter K = :r.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.RealZone"},{"category":"type","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.SpinOrbitalCouplingAmplitude","page":"Manual","text":"SpinOrbitalCouplingAmplitude{G<:PointGroup, N, D<:Number} <: Function\n\nSpin-orbital-coupling hopping amplitude under point group G. Matches a bond to the registered reference bonds via sign, which yields a spatial parity r = pm 1. The final SOC factor is -i cdot s cdot r, where s is the relative sign of the SOC coefficient lambda between bonds in the same (t lambda) group (precomputed by terms and stored in signs).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.SpinOrbitalCouplingAmplitude"},{"category":"type","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.Sublattice","page":"Manual","text":"Sublattice(nsublattice::Int)\n\nCallable that maps a lattice site index to its 1-based sublattice: (site - 1) % nsublattice + 1.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.Sublattice"},{"category":"type","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.SublatticeAmplitude","page":"Manual","text":"SublatticeAmplitude{G<:PointGroup, N, D<:Number} <: Function\n\nSpin-independent hopping amplitude. Matches a bond to the registered set of reference bonds via sign and returns 1 (match) or 0 (no match).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.SublatticeAmplitude"},{"category":"type","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.TanhCoulomb","page":"Manual","text":"TanhCoulomb(ϵ::Real, d::Real)\n\nGate-screened Coulomb: V(q) = 2π e² tanh(dₘ|q|) / (ϵ aₘ |q|) where dₘ = d/aₘ.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.TanhCoulomb"},{"category":"method","location":"manual/#QuantumLattices.Frameworks.Algorithm-Tuple{Symbol, BLTMD, NamedTuple{Names, T} where {Names, T<:(NTuple{N, Number} where N)}}","page":"Manual","text":"Algorithm(name::Symbol, bltmd::BLTMD, parameters::Parameters; kwargs...)\n\nConstruct an Algorithm with a BLTMD as the frontend.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"QuantumLattices.Frameworks.Algorithm"},{"category":"method","location":"manual/#QuantumLattices.Spatials.Lattice-Tuple{CommensurateBilayerHoneycomb, Symbol}","page":"Manual","text":"Lattice(moire::CommensurateBilayerHoneycomb, type::Symbol)\n\nGet the minimum unit of the top/bottom layer of a commensurate Moire superlattice composed of two layers of honeycomb lattices.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"QuantumLattices.Spatials.Lattice"},{"category":"method","location":"manual/#Base.angle-Tuple{CommensurateBilayerHoneycomb}","page":"Manual","text":"angle(moire::CommensurateBilayerHoneycomb) -> Float64\n\nGet the twist angle of a commensurate Moire superlattice composed of two layers of honeycomb lattices.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.angle"},{"category":"method","location":"manual/#Base.angle-Tuple{PointGroup}","page":"Manual","text":"angle(sym::PointGroup) -> Float64\nangle(::Type{G}) where {G<:PointGroup} -> Float64\n\nFundamental rotation angle of the point group in radians.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.angle"},{"category":"method","location":"manual/#Base.count-Tuple{CommensurateBilayerHoneycomb}","page":"Manual","text":"count(moire::CommensurateBilayerHoneycomb) -> Int\n\nCount the number of honeycomb unitcells contained in the unitcell of a commensurate Moire superlattice composed of two layers of honeycomb lattices.\n\nThe total number of atoms in the unitcell of the Moire superlattice is 4 times this result because of the AB sublattice and the top/bottom layer degrees of freedom.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.count"},{"category":"method","location":"manual/#Base.count-Tuple{MoireWannier}","page":"Manual","text":"count(wannier::MoireWannier) -> Int\n\nReturn the number of Wannier orbitals (n_rm band).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.count"},{"category":"method","location":"manual/#Base.in-Union{Tuple{G}, Tuple{QuantumLattices.Spatials.Bond, MoireNeighbors{G}}} where G<:PointGroup","page":"Manual","text":"in(bond::Bond, neighbors::MoireNeighbors) -> Bool\n\nCheck whether bond is symmetry-equivalent to any bond in neighbors.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.in"},{"category":"method","location":"manual/#Base.push!-Tuple{MoireNeighbors, QuantumLattices.Spatials.Bond}","page":"Manual","text":"push!(neighbors::MoireNeighbors, bond::Bond) -> MoireNeighbors\n\nPush bond if not symmetry-equivalent to an existing bond.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.push!"},{"category":"method","location":"manual/#Base.sign-Tuple{PointGroup, QuantumLattices.Spatials.Bond, QuantumLattices.Spatials.Bond, Int64}","page":"Manual","text":"sign(::Type{G}, ref::Bond, bond::Bond, nsublattice::Int; atol::Real=atol) where {G<:PointGroup} -> Int\nsign(sym::PointGroup, ref::Bond, bond::Bond, nsublattice::Int; atol::Real=atol) -> Int\n\nBond equivalence check under the point group G.\n\nEach concrete PointGroup subtype must implement Base.sign(::Type{G}, ref, bond, nsublattice) returning:\n\n+1: bond is symmetry-equivalent to ref in the forward direction.\n-1: bond is symmetry-equivalent to the reverse of ref.\n0: not equivalent.\n\nThe instance method sign(sym::PointGroup, ...) dispatches to the type-specific implementation via sign(typeof(sym), ...).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.sign"},{"category":"method","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.nsublattice-Tuple{MoireNeighbors}","page":"Manual","text":"nsublattice(neighbors::MoireNeighbors) -> Int\n\nNumber of sublattice sites per unit cell of the effective lattice.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.nsublattice"},{"category":"function","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.terms","page":"Manual","text":"terms(coulomb::CoulombIntegral, potential=BareCoulomb(1.0); order::Int=truncation(coulomb.wannier.lattice), ismodulatable::Bool=true, tol=atol) -> Tuple{Vararg{Term}}\n\nGenerate Coulomb interaction terms from a CoulombIntegral.\n\npotential is a callable potential(q::Real, aₘ::Real) -> Real, e.g. BareCoulomb(ϵ), ImageCoulomb(ϵ, d), TanhCoulomb(ϵ, d), or a user-defined function.\n\nAlgorithm\n\nPer-bond extraction — For each neighbor order k, the coefficient V = coulomb(R potential)i j is extracted for each symmetry-inequivalent bond independently. Each bond stored in MoireNeighbors is already inequivalent under the prescribed point group, so no within-group consistency assertion is needed.\nGrouping — Entries are grouped by V value across all pairs in the same shell.\nTerm construction — Each group yields a Coulomb term with SublatticeAmplitude for sublattice matching. Coulomb interaction is purely real, so there is no spin-orbital-coupling counterpart. Parameter names use V prefix (e.g., V₁, V₂).\nOnsite — Diagonal coulomb(0 potential)i i → Hubbard onsite repulsion with U prefix.\n\nNaming\n\nR > 0, nband = 1 or single group per shell: V₁, V₂, …\nR > 0, nband > 1 with multiple groups per shell: all pairs listed, e.g. V₁₍₁₋₂₊₂₋₃₎.\nR = 0 (onsite): U (all equal) or U₁, U₂, … (per-sublattice).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.terms"},{"category":"method","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.terms-Tuple{HoppingIntegral}","page":"Manual","text":"terms(hopping::HoppingIntegral; order::Int=truncation(hopping.wannier.lattice), ismodulatable::Bool=true, tol=atol) -> Tuple{Vararg{Term}}\n\nGenerate spin-independent and spin-orbital-coupling Hopping terms from a HoppingIntegral.\n\nAlgorithm\n\nPer-bond extraction — For each neighbor order k, the coefficient t + iλ = hopping(R)ij is extracted for each symmetry-inequivalent bond independently. Each bond stored in MoireNeighbors is already inequivalent under the prescribed point group, so no within-group consistency assertion is needed.\nGrouping — Entries are grouped by (t λ): t must match exactly (including sign), λ by magnitude. Relative signs between grouped λ values are precomputed.\nTerm construction — Each group yields two terms:\nt → Hopping with SublatticeAmplitude for sublattice matching.\nλ → Hopping with σᶻ coupling and SpinOrbitalCouplingAmplitude for spatial + sublattice matching.\nOnsite — Diagonal hopping(0)i i → Onsite chemical potentials.\n\nNaming\n\nnband = 1 and nband > 1 with single group per shell: t₁, λ₁, t₂, λ₂, …\nnband > 1 with multiple groups per shell: all pairs listed, e.g. t₁₍₁₋₂₊₂₋₃₎.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.terms"},{"category":"method","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.truncation-Tuple{MoireNeighbors}","page":"Manual","text":"truncation(neighbors::MoireNeighbors) -> Int\n\nMaximum neighbor order (kind) stored in neighbors.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.truncation"},{"category":"method","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.truncation-Tuple{MoireReciprocalLattice}","page":"Manual","text":"truncation(lattice::MoireReciprocalLattice) -> Int\n\nGet the truncation (number of shells) of a Moire reciprocal lattice.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.truncation"},{"category":"method","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.truncation-Tuple{MoireSuperlattice}","page":"Manual","text":"truncation(lattice::MoireSuperlattice) -> Int\n\nGet the truncation (number of shells) of a Moire superlattice.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.truncation"},{"category":"method","location":"manual/#MoireSuperlattices.vectors-Tuple{CommensurateBilayerHoneycomb}","page":"Manual","text":"vectors(moire::CommensurateBilayerHoneycomb) -> SVector{2, SVector{2, Float64}}\n\nGet the translation vectors of a commensurate Moire superlattice composed of two layers of honeycomb lattices.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MoireSuperlattices.vectors"},{"category":"method","location":"manual/#QuantumLattices.Spatials.bonds-Tuple{MoireNeighbors}","page":"Manual","text":"bonds(neighbors::MoireNeighbors) -> Vector{<:Bond}\nbonds(neighbors::MoireNeighbors, k::Int) -> Vector{<:Bond}\n\nBond access: all stored inequivalent bonds, or filtered by neighbor order k.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"QuantumLattices.Spatials.bonds"},{"category":"method","location":"manual/#QuantumLattices.Spatials.reciprocals-Tuple{MoireReciprocalLattice}","page":"Manual","text":"reciprocals(lattice::MoireReciprocalLattice) -> SVector{2, SVector{2, scalartype(lattice)}}\n\nGet the reciprocal translation vectors of a Moire reciprocal lattice.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"QuantumLattices.Spatials.reciprocals"},{"category":"method","location":"manual/#QuantumLattices.Spatials.reciprocals-Union{Tuple{PointGroup}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{PointGroup, Type{T}}} where T<:Number","page":"Manual","text":"reciprocals(sym::PointGroup, [T=Float64]) -> SVector{2, SVector{2, T}}\nreciprocals(::Type{G}, [T=Float64]) where {G<:PointGroup} -> SVector{2, SVector{2, T}}\n\nReciprocal-lattice translation vectors for the given point group.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"QuantumLattices.Spatials.reciprocals"},{"category":"section","location":"#MoireSuperlattices","page":"Home","text":"(Image: Stable) (Image: Dev) (Image: Build Status) (Image: Coverage) (Image: 996.icu) (Image: LICENSE) (Image: LICENSE) (Image: Code Style: Blue) (Image: ColPrac: Contributor's Guide on Collaborative Practices for Community Packages)","title":"MoireSuperlattices"},{"category":"section","location":"#Introduction","page":"Home","text":"This package aims at the construction of Moire Superlattices, acquisition of their effective models, and investigation of their low-energy physics, based on the QuantumLattices package and the TightBindingApproximation package.","title":"Introduction"},{"category":"section","location":"#Installation","page":"Home","text":"In Julia v1.10+, please type ] in the REPL to use the package mode, then type this command:\n\npkg> add MoireSuperlattices","title":"Installation"},{"category":"section","location":"#Getting-Started","page":"Home","text":"Examples of Moire Superlattice","title":"Getting Started"},{"category":"section","location":"#Note","page":"Home","text":"Due to the fast development of this package, releases with different minor version numbers are not guaranteed to be compatible with previous ones before the release of v1.0.0. Comments are welcomed in the issues.","title":"Note"},{"category":"section","location":"#Contact","page":"Home","text":"waltergu1989@gmail.com","title":"Contact"}]
}
